    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# How this works:\nIt is split up into 2 parts, The Random messages throughout the day and the chat mode\n\n## Random Messages\nis currently scheduled to run every 30 mins between 9am and 11pm, It fetches the last 2 hours of lifelogs as context, and chooses to respond to something, lifelogs are stored in limitless datatable (just for persistence) so it does not fill up context when conversations are spanning over multiple hours\n\n## Chat Mode\nIt has the context of the past 2 hours of transcripts and is able to search through lifelogs using the tool\n\n### Memory\nI also attempted to have the LLM persist memory of the user similar to what little I saw in the friend demos, I could have used a proper memory tool or RAG but I couldnt figure it out reliably. From my experience the LLM barely uses the memory tool to add memories, but it will always have the memories as context.",
        "height": 544,
        "width": 512,
        "color": 4
      },
